VERDICT -- rounds05
===================
R=2 PASSES ITS PRE-REGISTERED BAR; R=3 IS BEATEN BY IT AND DOES NOT SHIP.
Bar was: median absolute sum beats R=1 at 0.05, and no more than 5% lost on P1.

        R1 med      R2 med      d%      R3 med      d%   | R2 paired            R3 paired
  P1     631,046     556,718  -11.8%     636,883   +0.9% | -13.1 -11.8  -4.8   +0.9  +6.4  +8.9
  P3   4,745,895   4,887,024   +3.0%   4,859,009   +2.4% |  +3.0  +2.3  +3.0   +0.7  +4.1  +1.7
  P7     943,405   1,020,092   +8.1%   1,096,552  +16.2% | +16.8  +2.9 +12.3  +25.6 +31.4  +5.1
  P16  3,468,540   3,258,960   -6.0%   3,275,285   -5.6% |  -6.2  -3.9  -6.0   -5.6  -3.4  -5.6
  P27    907,800     729,804  -19.6%     730,112  -19.6% | -14.7 -15.5 -22.0  -25.4 -15.5 -12.6
  P33  1,192,334   1,220,871   +2.4%   1,202,515   +0.9% |  -0.7  +7.5 +26.7   -2.2 +10.3 +26.7
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  R2 median-sum 11,673,469 vs R1 11,889,020   -215,551  (-1.81%)
  R3 median-sum 11,800,356 vs R1 11,889,020    -88,664  (-0.75%)

THE KNOB WAS NEVER SHIPPED AND ITS RETIREMENT WAS INVALID.  `_R = max(1, int(os.environ.get(
"OGC_ROUNDS", "1")))` and nothing in the module sets it, though the comment at line 3367 asserts
otherwise.  The module's own note at the round loop records why the retiring measurement could not
have fired: at 60 s with the old reserve, wbudget ~47, _rb ~23 and reserve ~12, so "R=2 was never
two rounds there either."  RESFRAC 0.05 is what made a second round affordable -- reserve 3 s,
wbudget ~56, _rb ~28.

THE WINS ARE CONSISTENT AND THE LOSSES ARE NOT.  P1, P16 and P27 are 3/3 for R=2.  P33's paired
deltas are -0.7 / +7.5 / +26.7, which is not an effect.  The one real cost is P7 at +8.1%, positive
in all three replicates -- it wants depth, and at R=3 it loses 16.2%, which is what sinks R=3.

BUT THE BAND-WIDE MARGIN IS NOT RESOLVABLE AT THIS SAMPLE SIZE, AND THIS IS THE MEASUREMENT THAT
SAYS SO.  The SAME configuration -- P1, RESFRAC 0.05, R=1 -- gave different three-draw medians in
two experiments run hours apart on the same machine:

    rfship   537,403 / 518,803 / 631,046   median 537,403
    rounds05 631,046 / 631,046 / 584,609   median 631,046

A 17.4% gap between two medians of three draws each.  R=2's -1.81% median-sum sits well inside
that, so "R=2 wins across the band" is NOT established by this table.  Three-draw medians are not
the reliable instrument this study has been treating them as; they were enough to overturn P27's
single-draw +30.6%, and they are not enough to resolve two per cent.

P1 SURVIVES THE POOLED TEST, WHICH IS THE CLAIM WORTH MAKING.  Pooling all six R=1 draws at 0.05
from both experiments gives a median of 607,828 against R=2's 556,718 -- -8.4%, with R=2 ahead in
every rounds05 replicate.  That is the instance the hidden set is being played for, and it is the
narrow ground on which R=2 is worth shipping.
